A CI/CD pipeline diagram. Style: flowchart.

Pipeline stages triggered by a git push:
1. Developer pushes code to GitHub (feature branch)
2. GitHub Actions triggers the pipeline
3. Stage 1 — Build: install dependencies, compile TypeScript, check for errors
4. Stage 2 — Test: run unit tests, integration tests, generate coverage report
5. If tests fail: notify developer via Slack/email, pipeline stops
6. Stage 3 — Docker Build: build Docker image, tag with commit SHA
7. Stage 4 — Push: push image to Container Registry (e.g. AWS ECR or Docker Hub)
8. Stage 5 — Deploy to Staging: update Kubernetes deployment in staging namespace
9. Stage 6 — Smoke Test: run automated smoke tests against staging environment
10. If smoke tests pass: Deploy to Production (rolling update in k8s)
11. Monitor: send success notification, update deployment dashboard
